---@field metricNames? gcp.dfareporting_v5.StringList The list of names of metrics the report should include.
---@field customFloodlightVariables? gcp.dfareporting_v5.SortedDimensionList The list of custom floodlight variables the report should include.
---@field activityFilters? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DimensionValueList_ The list of 'dfa:activity' values to filter on.
---@field reportProperties? gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportPathToConversionCriteriaReportProperties The properties of the report.
---@field conversionDimensions? gcp.dfareporting_v5.SortedDimensionList The list of conversion dimensions the report should include.
---@field dateRange? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DateRange The date range this report should be run for.
---@field perInteractionDimensions? gcp.dfareporting_v5.SortedDimensionList The list of per interaction dimensions the report should include.
---@field floodlightConfigId? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DimensionValue The floodlight ID for which to show data in this report. All advertisers associated with that ID will automatically be added. The dimension of the value needs to be 'dfa:floodlightConfigId'.
---@field customRichMediaEvents? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DimensionValueList_ The list of custom rich media events to include.

---@class gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportPathToConversionCriteriaReportProperties
---@field maximumClickInteractions? number The maximum number of click interactions to include in the report. Advertisers currently paying for E2C reports get up to 200 (100 clicks, 100 impressions). If another advertiser in your network is paying for E2C, you can have up to 5 total exposures per report.
---@field maximumInteractionGap? number The maximum amount of time that can take place between interactions (clicks or impressions) by the same user. Valid values: 1-90.
---@field includeUnattributedIPConversions? boolean Include conversions that have no associated cookies and no exposures. It’s therefore impossible to know how the user was exposed to your ads during the lookback window prior to a conversion.
---@field clicksLookbackWindow? number CM360 checks to see if a click interaction occurred within the specified period of time before a conversion. By default the value is pulled from Floodlight or you can manually enter a custom value. Valid values: 1-90.
---@field maximumImpressionInteractions? number The maximum number of click interactions to include in the report. Advertisers currently paying for E2C reports get up to 200 (100 clicks, 100 impressions). If another advertiser in your network is paying for E2C, you can have up to 5 total exposures per report.
---@field includeUnattributedCookieConversions? boolean Include conversions of users with a DoubleClick cookie but without an exposure. That means the user did not click or see an ad from the advertiser within the Floodlight group, or that the interaction happened outside the lookback window.
---@field impressionsLookbackWindow? number CM360 checks to see if an impression interaction occurred within the specified period of time before a conversion. By default the value is pulled from Floodlight or you can manually enter a custom value. Valid values: 1-90.
---@field pivotOnInteractionPath? boolean Enable pivoting on interaction path.
---@field includeAttributedIPConversions? boolean Deprecated: has no effect.

---@class gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportReachCriteria
---@field customRichMediaEvents? gcp.dfareporting_v5.CustomRichMediaEvents Custom Rich Media Events group.
---@field metricNames? gcp.dfareporting_v5.StringList The list of names of metrics the report should include.
---@field dateRange? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DateRange The date range this report should be run for.
---@field activities? gcp.dfareporting_v5.Activities Activity group.
---@field dimensions? gcp.dfareporting_v5.SortedDimensionList The list of dimensions the report should include.
---@field dimensionFilters? gcp.dfareporting_v5.DimensionValueList_ The list of filters on which dimensions are filtered. Filters for different dimensions are ANDed, filters for the same dimension are grouped together and ORed.
---@field reachByFrequencyMetricNames? gcp.dfareporting_v5.StringList The list of names of Reach By Frequency metrics the report should include.

---@class gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportSchedule
---@field every? number Defines every how many days, weeks or months the report should be run. Needs to be set when "repeats" is either "DAILY", "WEEKLY" or "MONTHLY".
---@field repeatsOnWeekDays? gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRepeatsOnWeekDaysItemEnumList List of week days "WEEKLY" on which scheduled reports should run.
---@field timezone? string The timezone when the report will run.
---@field repeats? string The interval for which the report is repeated. Note: - "DAILY" also requires field "every" to be set. - "WEEKLY" also requires fields "every" and "repeatsOnWeekDays" to be set. - "MONTHLY" also requires fields "every" and "runsOnDayOfMonth" to be set.
---@field runsOnDayOfMonth? gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRunsOnDayOfMonthEnum|string Enum to define for "MONTHLY" scheduled reports whether reports should be repeated on the same day of the month as "startDate" or the same day of the week of the month. Example: If 'startDate' is Monday, April 2nd 2012 (2012-04-02), "DAY_OF_MONTH" would run subsequent reports on the 2nd of every Month, and "WEEK_OF_MONTH" would run subsequent reports on the first Monday of the month.
---@field active? boolean Whether the schedule is active or not. Must be set to either true or false.
---@field startDate? string
---@field expirationDate? string

---@alias gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRepeatsOnWeekDaysItemEnum "SUNDAY"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"

---@alias gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRepeatsOnWeekDaysItemEnumList (gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRepeatsOnWeekDaysItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportScheduleRunsOnDayOfMonthEnum "DAY_OF_MONTH"|"WEEK_OF_MONTH"

---@alias gcp.dfareporting_v5.ReportTypeEnum "STANDARD"|"REACH"|"PATH_TO_CONVERSION"|"FLOODLIGHT"|"CROSS_MEDIA_REACH"

